{"title":"Keter Shem Tob Reader","content":{"files":{"Main.dc.html":"\u003c!doctype html>\n\u003chtml>\n\u003chead>\n  \u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  \u003cscript src=\"./support.js\">\u003c/script>\n\u003c/head>\n\u003cbody>\n\u003cx-dc>\n\u003chelmet>\n  \u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300;0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\">\n  \u003cstyle>\n    body { margin:0; background:#F6F4EE; color:#1C1A15; font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; }\n    a { color:#8A6A1E; } a:hover { color:#6F5418; }\n    .mono { font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',ui-monospace,monospace; }\n    .he { font-family:'Taamey Frank CLM','SBL Hebrew','Noto Serif Hebrew','Arial Hebrew',serif;\n      direction:rtl; unicode-bidi:isolate; }\n  \u003c/style>\n\u003c/helmet>\n\u003cdiv style=\"width:880px; padding:52px 56px; background:#F6F4EE\">\n  \u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; border-bottom:1px solid #CFC8B6; padding-bottom:16px; margin-bottom:34px\">\n    \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:17px; letter-spacing:.14em; color:#8A6A1E\">PRINTED 18\u003c/span>\n    \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:15px; color:#6F6A5D\">London · Amsterdam · S–T–E\u003c/span>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003ch2 style=\"font-size:31px; font-weight:600; line-height:1.32; margin:0 0 24px\">From when the title of \"Bar Mitsvah\" became known for a lad who has re\u003c/h2>\n  \u003cp style=\"font-size:27px; line-height:1.7; margin:0 0 34px\">### From when the title of \"Bar Mitsvah\" became known for a lad who has reached the age of thirteen years and one day [32]\n\n**The Blessings of the Dawn, like white wool**\n\nAnd it contains two se'ifim.\n\n(1) In the morning blessings, differences have arisen between the Nusah of London and Amsterdam and the Nusah of Erets Yisrael, \u003csup class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:.55em; color:#8A6A1E; vertical-align:super\">33\u003c/sup>\u003c/p>\n  \u003cdiv style=\"border-top:1px solid #DCD7C9; padding-top:24px\">\n    \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:.16em; color:#8A6A1E; margin:0 0 18px\">NOTES IN THE MARGIN\u003c/p>\n    \u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; margin-bottom:20px\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:15px; color:#8A6A1E; padding-top:3px\">32\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.55; color:#3B372E\">This expression \"Bar Mitsvah\" became known through the rabbis of Ashkenaz. And it is borrowed from the words of the Gema…\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; margin-bottom:20px\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:15px; color:#8A6A1E; padding-top:3px\">33\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.55; color:#3B372E\">With regard to the wording of London and Amsterdam, who mention \"Lord of all souls\" at the end — which is not so the Min…\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:.16em; color:#8A6A1E; margin:30px 0 14px\">THE HEBREW\u003c/p>\n    \u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:14px; padding:11px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #DCD7C9\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"he\" style=\"font-size:25px; line-height:1.8\">רִבּוֹן כָּל־הַמַּעֲשִׂים אֲדוֹן כָּל־הַ\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D; white-space:nowrap\">edot hamizrach\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:14px; padding:11px 0; border-bottom:1px solid #DCD7C9\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"he\" style=\"font-size:25px; line-height:1.8\">שאתה הוא רבו־ן כל־המעשים\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D; white-space:nowrap\">london sp\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\n\u003c/div>\u003c/x-dc>\n\u003c/body>\n\u003c/html>\n","Comparison.dc.html":"\u003c!doctype html>\n\u003chtml>\n\u003chead>\n  \u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  \u003cscript src=\"./support.js\">\u003c/script>\n\u003c/head>\n\u003cbody>\n\u003cx-dc>\n\u003chelmet>\n  \u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300;0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\">\n  \u003cstyle>\n    body { margin:0; background:#F6F4EE; color:#1C1A15; font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; }\n    a { color:#8A6A1E; } a:hover { color:#6F5418; }\n    .mono { font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',ui-monospace,monospace; }\n    .he { font-family:'Taamey Frank CLM','SBL Hebrew','Noto Serif Hebrew','Arial Hebrew',serif;\n      direction:rtl; unicode-bidi:isolate; }\n  \u003c/style>\n\u003c/helmet>\n\u003cdiv style=\"width:880px; padding:52px 56px; background:#F6F4EE\">\n  \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:16px; letter-spacing:.14em; color:#8A6A1E; margin:0 0 10px\">WHERE THEY DIFFER\u003c/p>\n  \u003ch2 style=\"font-size:38px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px\">Morning blessings\u003c/h2>\n  \u003cp style=\"font-size:21px; color:#6F6A5D; margin:0 0 34px; font-family:system-ui\">Every place Gaguine sets these two against each other.\u003c/p>\n  \u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; gap:20px; margin-bottom:20px\">\n    \u003cdiv style=\"flex:1; min-width:0; padding:26px 28px; background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD7C9; border-radius:12px\">\n      \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:.12em; color:#3F6B8C; margin:0 0 16px\">LONDON &amp; AMSTERDAM\u003c/p>\n      \u003cp style=\"font-size:23px; line-height:1.6; margin:0\">Master of all works, ruling over all creatures\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n    \u003cdiv style=\"flex:1; min-width:0; padding:26px 28px; background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD7C9; border-radius:12px\">\n      \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:.12em; color:#7A4A7A; margin:0 0 16px\">ERETS YISRAEL · S–T–E\u003c/p>\n      \u003cp style=\"font-size:23px; line-height:1.6; margin:0\">… and they add \u003cstrong>Lord of all souls\u003c/strong>, and \u003cstrong>living and enduring\u003c/strong>\u003c/p>\u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; padding:18px 22px; background:#EFECE3; border-radius:11px\">\n    \u003cspan class=\"he\" style=\"font-size:27px\">רִבּוֹן כָּל־הַמַּעֲשִׂים אֲדוֹן כָּל־הַנְּש\u003c/span>\n    \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D\">Edot HaMizrach\u003c/span>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:16px; color:#6F6A5D; margin:30px 0 0\">12 more places these two diverge →\u003c/p>\n\u003c/div>\u003c/x-dc>\n\u003c/body>\n\u003c/html>\n","Deck.dc.html":"\u003c!doctype html>\n\u003chtml>\n\u003chead>\n  \u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  \u003cscript src=\"./support.js\">\u003c/script>\n\u003c/head>\n\u003cbody>\n\u003cx-dc>\n\u003chelmet>\n  \u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300;0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\">\n  \u003cstyle>\n    body { margin:0; background:#F6F4EE; color:#1C1A15; font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; }\n    a { color:#8A6A1E; } a:hover { color:#6F5418; }\n    .mono { font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',ui-monospace,monospace; }\n    .he { font-family:'Taamey Frank CLM','SBL Hebrew','Noto Serif Hebrew','Arial Hebrew',serif;\n      direction:rtl; unicode-bidi:isolate; }\n  \u003c/style>\n\u003c/helmet>\n\u003cdiv style=\"width:880px; padding:52px 56px; background:#F6F4EE\">\n  \u003ch2 style=\"font-size:38px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 10px\">1,035 customs\u003c/h2>\n  \u003cp style=\"font-size:21px; color:#6F6A5D; margin:0 0 28px; font-family:system-ui\">Sift rather than scroll.\u003c/p>\n  \u003cdiv style=\"display:flex; gap:10px; margin-bottom:26px\">\n    \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:16px; padding:11px 20px; border-radius:99px; background:#8A6A1E; color:#fff\">All\u003c/span>\n    \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:16px; padding:11px 20px; border-radius:99px; border:1px solid #CFC8B6; color:#6F6A5D\">London\u003c/span>\n    \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:16px; padding:11px 20px; border-radius:99px; border:1px solid #CFC8B6; color:#6F6A5D\">Amsterdam\u003c/span>\n  \u003c/div>\n  \u003cdiv style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap:18px\">\u003cdiv style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD7C9; border-radius:13px; padding:22px 22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; min-height:190px\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.1em; color:#8A6A1E\">VERSES AND PRAYERS\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan style=\"flex:1; font-size:21px; line-height:1.42\">The verse \"But as for me, in the abundance of Thy lovingkindness\"\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D\">printed 2\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD7C9; border-radius:13px; padding:22px 22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; min-height:190px\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.1em; color:#8A6A1E\">THE WASHING OF HANDS\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan style=\"flex:1; font-size:21px; line-height:1.42\">Why the Sages ordained the washing of hands with the term *netiláh* and not *r\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D\">printed 4\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD7C9; border-radius:13px; padding:22px 22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; min-height:190px\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.1em; color:#8A6A1E\">THE WASHING OF HANDS\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan style=\"flex:1; font-size:21px; line-height:1.42\">Ḳaddésh uReḥats — why in the second the term *reḥitsáh* is used\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D\">printed 4\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003cdiv style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD7C9; border-radius:13px; padding:22px 22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; min-height:190px\">\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.1em; color:#8A6A1E\">TEPHILLÉEN\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan style=\"flex:1; font-size:21px; line-height:1.42\">The donning of the Talét before the Tephilléen\u003c/span>\n  \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:14px; color:#6F6A5D\">printed 6\u003c/span>\u003c/div>\u003c/div>\n\u003c/div>\u003c/x-dc>\n\u003c/body>\n\u003c/html>\n","Quiet.dc.html":"\u003c!doctype html>\n\u003chtml>\n\u003chead>\n  \u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\">\n  \u003cscript src=\"./support.js\">\u003c/script>\n\u003c/head>\n\u003cbody>\n\u003cx-dc>\n\u003chelmet>\n  \u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300;0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\">\n  \u003cstyle>\n    body { margin:0; background:#F6F4EE; color:#1C1A15; font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,serif; }\n    a { color:#8A6A1E; } a:hover { color:#6F5418; }\n    .mono { font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',ui-monospace,monospace; }\n    .he { font-family:'Taamey Frank CLM','SBL Hebrew','Noto Serif Hebrew','Arial Hebrew',serif;\n      direction:rtl; unicode-bidi:isolate; }\n  \u003c/style>\n\u003c/helmet>\n\u003cdiv style=\"width:880px; min-height:760px; background:#131209; color:#F0EBDE; display:flex; justify-content:center\">\n  \u003cdiv style=\"width:640px; padding:88px 0 70px\">\n    \u003cp class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:16px; letter-spacing:.18em; color:#918A7A; margin:0 0 46px\">18\u003c/p>\n    \u003ch2 style=\"font-size:30px; font-weight:400; line-height:1.38; margin:0 0 30px\">From when the title of \"Bar Mitsvah\" became known for a lad who has re\u003c/h2>\n    \u003cp style=\"font-size:27px; line-height:1.8; margin:0; color:#E6E0D2\">### From when the title of \"Bar Mitsvah\" became known for a lad who has reached the age of thirteen years and one day [32]\n\n**The Blessings of the Dawn, like white wool**\n\nAnd it contains two se'ifim.\n\n(1) In the morning blessings, differences have arisen between the Nusah of London and Amsterdam and the Nusah of Erets Yisrael, Syria, Egypt and Turkey. In the Nusah of London and Amsterdam: that Thou art the Master of all works\u003c/p>\n    \u003cdiv style=\"margin-top:60px; padding-top:22px; border-top:1px solid #332F26; display:flex; gap:30px\">\n      \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:15px; color:#918A7A\">3 notes\u003c/span>\n      \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:15px; color:#918A7A\">2 Hebrew quotations\u003c/span>\n      \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:15px; color:#C9A54D\">the page itself ↗\u003c/span>\n    \u003c/div>\n  \u003c/div>\n\u003c/div>\u003c/x-dc>\n\u003c/body>\n\u003c/html>\n","canvas.json":"{\n  \"artboards\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"Main.dc.html\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"w\": 880,\n      \"h\": 900,\n      \"title\": \"A · The apparatus\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"Comparison.dc.html\",\n      \"x\": 990,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"w\": 880,\n      \"h\": 660,\n      \"title\": \"B · The comparison\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"Deck.dc.html\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 1030,\n      \"w\": 880,\n      \"h\": 700,\n      \"title\": \"C · The deck\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"Quiet.dc.html\",\n      \"x\": 990,\n      \"y\": 1030,\n      \"w\": 880,\n      \"h\": 760,\n      \"title\": \"D · The quiet page\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"annotations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"brief\",\n      \"x\": -330,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"w\": 270,\n      \"text\": \"Four directions for the reader.\\n\\nThe live site's own tokens and real text from printed p18.\\n\\nPic